                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_02\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix adds an early-return guard `if (udts.isEmpty()) { return; }` at the top of `loadUserTypes` and simplifies the trailing recursive call from `if (notLoaded.size() > 0) { loadUserTypes(notLoaded, ks); }` to an unconditional `loadUserTypes(notLoaded, ks);`. The root cause is the check `if (notLoaded.size() == udts.size()) { throw new RuntimeException(...) }`: when `udts` is empty (a keyspace with no user-defined types), `notLoaded.size()` is 0 and `udts.size()` is 0, so `0 == 0` is true and the method incorrectly throws a RuntimeException instead of simply doing nothing, breaking the loader for keyspaces without UDTs.\n\nCandidate_01 creates the initial `BulkLoader.java` (and related sstableloader/build.xml scaffolding) but does not contain the `loadUserTypes` method at all \u2014 that logic doesn't exist yet in this commit.\n\nCandidate_02 introduces the entire `loadUserTypes`/`getCql3Type` UDT-loading machinery, including the exact problematic code: `if (notLoaded.size() == udts.size()) { throw new RuntimeException(\"Unable to load user types \" + notLoaded); }` with no prior guard for an empty `udts` collection. This is precisely the bug the fix commit addresses, and it is the first commit where this code exists.\n\nCandidate_03 is actually the fix commit itself (its diff is identical to fix_commit_diff.txt), so it removes/patches the bug rather than introducing it.\n\nTherefore candidate_02 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
                }
